.TH COMPILE-VA-MODELS 1 "March 2026" "IHP macOS Toolkit" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
compile-va-models.sh \- Compile Verilog-A models to OSDI format
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B compile-va-models.sh
[\fB\-\-pdk\-root\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-\-force\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B compile-va-models.sh
compiles Verilog-A (.va) device models to OSDI (.osdi) format for use
with ngspice.

The script uses OpenVAF inside Docker to perform compilation, automatically
discovering all .va files in the PDK and compiling them if .osdi versions
don't exist or are outdated.
.SH WHY COMPILATION IS NEEDED
Verilog-A models (.va files) are source code that must be compiled before
ngspice can use them:
.PP
.TS
tab(|);
l l l.
Format|Type|Usage
_
.va|Source code|Human-readable model
.osdi|Compiled binary|Loaded by ngspice
.EE
.PP
The IHP SG13G2 PDK includes important Verilog-A models:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
PSP103 (MOSFET model)
.IP \(bu 2
HICUM Level 2 (HBT/BJT model)
.IP \(bu 2
Various device models
.RE
.PP
Without compilation, these models cannot be used in simulations.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-pdk\-root " path"
Specify PDK root directory explicitly.
If not provided, uses $PDK_ROOT environment variable.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Force recompilation even if .osdi files exist and are newer than .va sources.
.SH PREREQUISITES
.SS Environment
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
# Configure environment first
source $ASIC_DESIGN_ROOT/projets/env/zshrc_elec

# Verify
echo $PDK_ROOT
.EE
.in
.SS Docker
Docker Desktop must be running:
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
docker info
.EE
.in
.SS PDK Installed
IHP-Open-PDK must be present:
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
ls $PDK_ROOT/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/verilog-a/
.EE
.in
.SH USAGE
.SS Basic Usage
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
compile-va-models.sh
.EE
.in
.PP
Compiles all .va models found in $PDK_ROOT.
.SS Specify PDK Path
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
compile-va-models.sh --pdk-root /path/to/IHP-Open-PDK
.EE
.in
.SS Force Recompilation
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
compile-va-models.sh --force
.EE
.in
.PP
Useful after PDK updates or OpenVAF version changes.
.SH WHAT IT DOES
.SS Discovery Phase
.RS 4
.IP 1. 3
Searches for .va files in $PDK_ROOT/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/verilog-a/
.IP 2.
Lists all found models
.IP 3.
Checks for existing .osdi files
.RE
.SS Compilation Phase
For each .va file:
.RS 4
.IP 1. 3
Checks if .osdi exists and is newer
.IP 2.
Skips if up-to-date (unless --force)
.IP 3.
Compiles using OpenVAF in Docker
.IP 4.
Verifies .osdi was created
.IP 5.
Reports success or failure
.RE
.SS Summary
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
Total models found
.IP \(bu 2
Models compiled
.IP \(bu 2
Models skipped (up-to-date)
.IP \(bu 2
Compilation failures
.RE
.SH OUTPUT
.SS Successful Compilation
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
=== Verilog-A Model Compilation ===

PDK: /Users/you/Electronics/outils/IHP-Open-PDK
Target: ihp-sg13g2

Discovering Verilog-A models...
Found 3 models:
  - psp103/psp103_nqs.va
  - hicuml2/hicumL2V2p4p0_release.va
  - bjt/bjt504t.va

Compiling models...

[1/3] psp103_nqs.va
  ✓ Compiled successfully
  → psp103_nqs.osdi

[2/3] hicumL2V2p4p0_release.va
  ↻ Skipping (up-to-date)

[3/3] bjt504t.va
  ✓ Compiled successfully
  → bjt504t.osdi

Summary:
  Total:    3 models
  Compiled: 2 models
  Skipped:  1 model
  Failed:   0 models

✓ Compilation complete
.EE
.in
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All compilations successful (or skipped if up-to-date)
.TP
.B 1
One or more compilations failed
.TP
.B 2
Environment error (PDK_ROOT not set, Docker not running)
.SH WHEN TO RUN
Run compilation:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
After initial PDK installation
.IP \(bu 2
After PDK updates (git pull)
.IP \(bu 2
If .osdi files are missing or corrupted
.IP \(bu 2
After Docker image updates (new OpenVAF version)
.RE
.PP
Typically, compilation is needed only once after PDK installation.
.SH COMPILATION TIME
Typical compilation times per model:
.PP
.TS
tab(|);
l l.
Model|Time
_
PSP103 (MOSFET)|30-60 seconds
HICUM L2 (HBT)|60-120 seconds
Simple models|10-30 seconds
.TE
.PP
Total compilation time for IHP SG13G2: ~2-5 minutes.
.SH TROUBLESHOOTING
.SS Docker not running
.PP
.B Error:
Cannot connect to Docker daemon
.PP
.B Fix:
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
# Launch Docker Desktop and wait
docker info
.EE
.in
.SS PDK_ROOT not set
.PP
.B Error:
PDK_ROOT environment variable not set
.PP
.B Fix:
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
source $ASIC_DESIGN_ROOT/projets/env/zshrc_elec
.EE
.in
.PP
Or use --pdk-root flag.
.SS Compilation fails
.PP
.B Symptoms:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
Error messages from OpenVAF
.IP \(bu 2
.osdi file not created
.IP \(bu 2
Parser errors in .va file
.RE
.PP
.B Possible causes:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
Corrupted .va file
.IP \(bu 2
OpenVAF version incompatibility
.IP \(bu 2
Verilog-A syntax errors
.RE
.PP
.B Fix:
.RS 4
.IP 1. 3
Try --force to recompile
.IP 2.
Update Docker image:
.B docker pull hpretl/iic-osic-tools:latest
.IP 3.
Check PDK integrity:
.B git status
in PDK directory
.IP 4.
Report issue if .va file is from official PDK
.RE
.SS Permission denied
.PP
.B Error:
Cannot write .osdi file
.PP
.B Fix:
Check write permissions on PDK directory:
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
ls -la $PDK_ROOT/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/verilog-a/
.EE
.in
.SS Models not found in simulation
.PP
After successful compilation, if ngspice still cannot find models:
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
# Verify .osdi files exist
find $PDK_ROOT -name "*.osdi"

# Check netlist uses correct paths
# Should use: /pdk/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/verilog-a/...
.EE
.in
.SH COMPILED OUTPUT LOCATION
.PP
.osdi files are created in the same directory as their source .va files:
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
$PDK_ROOT/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/verilog-a/
├── psp103/
│   ├── psp103_nqs.va         (source)
│   └── psp103_nqs.osdi       (compiled)
├── hicuml2/
│   ├── hicumL2V2p4p0_release.va
│   └── hicumL2V2p4p0_release.osdi
└── ...
.EE
.in
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $TOOLKIT_ROOT/scripts/compile-va-models.sh
The compilation script
.TP
.I $PDK_ROOT/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/verilog-a/
Directory containing .va source files
.TP
.I $PDK_ROOT/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/verilog-a/*/*.osdi
Compiled model files
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PDK_ROOT
Path to IHP-Open-PDK (required)
.TP
.B PDK
PDK name, typically "ihp-sg13g2" (optional)
.SH ADVANCED USAGE
.SS Compile Specific Model
.PP
The script compiles all models. To compile one specific model manually:
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
cd $PDK_ROOT/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/verilog-a/psp103

docker run --rm \\
  -v "$PWD:/work" \\
  -w /work \\
  hpretl/iic-osic-tools:latest \\
  openvaf psp103_nqs.va -o psp103_nqs.osdi
.EE
.in
.SS Check OpenVAF Version
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
docker run --rm hpretl/iic-osic-tools:latest openvaf --version
.EE
.in
